{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## OPERATOR POLICY DECISION (authoritative) — this ticket IS a defect; the docs are what is wrong\n\nThe operator has ruled on this directly. Verbatim:\n\n> \"Certification environment should not currently be a gate. Any certification is as good as any other certification right now. Limited to a trusted set of environments is a future feature, but not currently in use.\"\n\nThis SUPERSEDES the prior `/rebar-debug` Phase 1 comment on this ticket, which classified the\nbehavior `intended-behavior` on the authority of `docs/manifest-signing.md:30`,\n`docs/plan-review-gate.md:57/:1122-1125/:1536/:1552`, and\n`docs/migrations/hmac-opcert-removal.md:74-80`. Those documents encode the *future* trusted-set\nrestriction as if it were live policy — **that encoding is the defect**, in code and in the docs\nalike. Do not re-litigate this decision against them; they are being corrected as part of this\nfix.\n\n### What the decision does and does not say\n\n- **Environment/principal identity must not, by itself, cause a refusal.** A cryptographically\n  valid certificate is a certification regardless of which environment minted it.\n- **\"Not gated on environment\" is not \"gated on nothing.\"** A signature that does not verify is\n  still not a certification. `verify-signature`'s `mismatch` and `unsigned` verdicts keep their\n  exact meaning, and an altered/forged envelope is still refused.\n- **The trusted-set restriction is DEFERRED, not deleted.** `verify.require_environment` +\n  `verify.opcert_enforce_since` (both unset in this project) and `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`\n  remain the opt-in enforcement seam for the future feature. They must not gate when unset, and\n  must keep working unchanged when set.\n\n### Precedent\n\nThis is the same call the operator already made for the bugfix-size gate in bug\n`stuffed-custommade-nuthatch` (846b): \"the attestation check must NOT gate on the SOURCE of\ncertification. It gates ONLY on the FACT that an attested plan review has been completed\" —\nimplemented there by deleting the pinned-keyring lookup from `bugfix_size_gate.py`. This ticket\nextends the identical policy to the claim gate's op-cert verification path.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787961358959942708,"uuid":"454fe295-50b4-4cdc-9eb5-b6370b9c2def"}